      "kind": "check",
      "context": "A product team wants a better checkout page. Three people wrote a goal for it.",
      "question": "Which statement is a UX goal?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "Redesign the payment button.",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "reason": "This sounds like a goal, but it names a design change. It tells the designer what to make, not what should change for people. A goal would say what people do or feel differently."
        },
        {
          "text": "More people finish paying on the first attempt.",
          "isCorrect": true,
          "reason": "This names a change in what people do: they finish paying without retrying. It says nothing about which button, bar or screen should cause it."
        },
        {
          "text": "Add a saved-card option to checkout.",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "reason": "This names a feature to build. It is a solution, so it doesn't say what should change for the shopper."
        }
      ],
      "image": null,
      "visual": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "activity",
      "template": "findError",
      "content": "{\"prompt\":\"Find the step where the AI assistant's answer goes wrong.\",\"fields\":{\"author\":\"ai\",\"problem\":\"Turn these interview notes into a UX goal for our food delivery app. Notes: 6 of 8 people closed the app when the delivery fee showed up late in checkout.\",\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"The notes say people close the app when the delivery fee appears late in checkout.\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"The goal is: show the delivery fee on the home screen.\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Success measure: the share of people who show the fee on the home screen rises to 100%.\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Summary: the goal is to show the delivery fee on the home screen, measured by the share of screens that show it.\"}],\"errorStepId\":\"s2\",\"why\":\"Step 2 names a design (showing the fee on the home screen), not a change in people's experience. The notes describe people who leave when the fee appears late. A goal should say that fewer people abandon orders at that point.\",\"correction\":\"Fewer people close the app at checkout after seeing the delivery fee.\"},\"check\":{\"kind\":\"interaction\",\"explanation\":\"Step 2 is the wrong step because it names a solution. Steps 3 and 4 then measure and summarize that solution, so the whole goal is off.\"},\"image\":{\"prompt\":\"A simple flat illustration of a phone showing a food delivery checkout screen, with a small delivery fee line appearing late and a thought bubble with a question mark over an AI assistant chat panel listing four numbered steps.\",\"alt\":\"A phone checkout screen with a late delivery fee line next to an AI assistant's four numbered steps.\"}}"
    },
    {
      "kind": "check",
      "context": "A banking app team reads support tickets. Many customers write: \"I can't find where to change my card limit.\"",
      "question": "Which option is the UX goal?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "Add a Card Limits tab to the main menu.",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "reason": "This names a menu change, which is a solution. It tells the team what to build, not what should change for customers."
        },
        {
          "text": "Fewer customers contact support to find their card limit settings.",
          "isCorrect": true,
          "reason": "This names a change in customer behavior: fewer support contacts about finding the setting. It leaves the design open."
        },
        {
          "text": "Move the card limit setting to the top of the screen.",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "reason": "This is a design move. It assumes the location is the problem, so it is a solution written as a change to the screen."
        },
        {
          "text": "Redesign the card settings page with a search bar.",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "reason": "This proposes a redesign with a specific feature. It is a solution, even though it sounds like a goal."
        }
      ],
      "image": null,
      "visual": null
    }
  ],
  "summary": [
    "A UX goal names the change in people's experience, such as fewer people giving up at payment.",
    "A proposed solution names a design, such as adding a progress bar, and it may or may not cause the change.",
    "Before you design, check that the goal names a change and leaves the design open."
  ]
}

